### 2C — `behavior: "queue"` on all InjectAgentMessage sends

**Why:** Deepgram returns `INJECT_AGENT_MESSAGE_DURING_AGENT_SPEECH` warning (non-fatal but wastes the inject) when OBI is speaking. Adding `behavior: "queue"` queues it instead of dropping.

**Find all calls:** `agentWs.send(JSON.stringify({ type: "InjectAgentMessage"`  
**Add to each:** `behavior: "queue"` field in the payload object.  
**Exception:** The proactive greeting (SettingsApplied handler) — keep as `"default"` since we WANT it dropped if OBI is already speaking.

### 2D — FAILED_TO_SPEAK / FAILED_TO_THINK error handling

**In the message handler switch/if chain**, add:
```js
} else if (msg.type === 'Error') {
  if (msg.code === 'FAILED_TO_SPEAK' || msg.code === 'FAILED_TO_THINK') {
    bubble('obi', '[Connection issue — please refresh if OBI stops responding]');
  }
  reportClientError('DEEPGRAM_ERROR', { code: msg.code, description: msg.description });
}
